### Run these from IntelliJ or the VS Code REST Client. Ports: 8080 = monolith or shop, 8081 = warehouse.

### Users
GET http://localhost:8080/api/users

### Products (on the warehouse when you run the split)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/products?category=appliances

### Stock
GET http://localhost:8080/api/stock

### Place an order: Carol buys 2 coffee grinders
POST http://localhost:8080/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{"userId": 3, "productId": 2, "quantity": 2}

### Out of stock: 409 OUT_OF_STOCK from inventory
POST http://localhost:8080/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{"userId": 1, "productId": 4, "quantity": 1}

### Not enough money: 409 INSUFFICIENT_FUNDS from payments (Bob has 50.00)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{"userId": 2, "productId": 1, "quantity": 1}

### Unknown product: 404 PRODUCT_NOT_FOUND from catalog
POST http://localhost:8080/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{"userId": 1, "productId": 42, "quantity": 1}

### Orders and payments
GET http://localhost:8080/api/orders

###
GET http://localhost:8080/api/payments

### Every module call, tagged by module, method, mode and outcome
GET http://localhost:8080/actuator/metrics/module.switch.call

### Call the warehouse's internal port directly, the way the shop does (split mode only)
POST http://localhost:9081/catalog/CatalogApi/getProduct
Content-Type: application/json
X-Module-Switch-Token: local-dev-secret

{"id": 1}
